::  name       dark-mode layer
::  shape      a style: layer that sets the ground (paper/ink) only — no accent
::  invariant  each style token is `key value` flat Bron; both stay warm/low-blue
::  example    Bark page, Flax ink — the mode, with the accent left to another layer
::  readers    brush_parse.rye → tokens.resolve_stack → mantra_browser_theme_stack
::  nib        surface-wade1-mode-dark-v0
::
::  A .brush *mode* layer: it names only the ground of the surface — a dark page and
::  a light ink — and deliberately leaves `head` (the living-edge accent) for a
::  separate accent layer to set. Stacking a mode layer and an accent layer proves
::  the WADE1 cascade composes independent authored layers, top wins, base inherits.
::  Tongue: Glow · Bron · TAME · Radiant. Never JS · HTML · CSS · JSON.
::
::  at-nib:     mantra-graph-dark-mode
::  present:    Frame
::  max-lines:  8
::  style:
::    paper 0xFF2B2620
::    ink 0xFFF2ECDF
::  lines:
::    mantra graph, dark mode layer
::  refuse:     src/web · Wasm/Web backend · CSS rail · a { } stylesheet
